  "scope": "Follow-up experiments on newer main. The existing PR source and SUMMARY.json still describe the original field-clone candidate on 630a074. No source change is promoted by this follow-up.",
  "reproduction": "Start each trial from the pinned newer main with the same recipe and dependencies as SUMMARY.json. For 02 replace only sweep_fees.rs with the exact upstream PR1548 file. For 03 apply the recorded replacement and append the helper. For 04 remove only the helper inline(always) attribute, retaining its newline. Build each in a separate directory; score with the unchanged official scorer and target metric. Original allocation capture and inventory are the same pinned inputs as SUMMARY.json.",
  "first_mutation": {
    "old": "  (true,true)=>match Rent::get(){\n   Ok(rent)=>{let minimum=rent.minimum_balance(0);if a.recipient.lamports()<minimum{crate::legacy_buy::native_payments::transfer(a.system_program.as_ref(),&a.payer,a.recipient.as_ref(),minimum)}else{Ok(())}}\n   Err(e)=>Err(e.into()),\n  }?,",
    "new": "  (true,true)=>rent_result(a,Rent::get())?,\n\n\n",
    "append": "#[inline(always)]\nfn rent_result<'info>(a:&mut SweepFees<'info>,rent:std::result::Result<Rent,anchor_lang::solana_program::program_error::ProgramError>)->Result<()>{\n match rent{\n  Ok(rent)=>{let minimum=rent.minimum_balance(0);if a.recipient.lamports()<minimum{crate::legacy_buy::native_payments::transfer(a.system_program.as_ref(),&a.payer,a.recipient.as_ref(),minimum)}else{Ok(())}}\n  Err(e)=>Err(e.into()),\n }\n}\n",
    "candidate_sha256": "9474f1418538a3caea2e0466c2a3e93ca1befebc019b740560ef9fca7981fe80",
    "hypothesis": "A by-value Rent Result boundary may materialize the original pre-branch Rent copy while retaining the shared top-up/error Result join and lifetime-marked storage. Unlike the earlier helper, Rent::get stays in execute."
  },
  "second_mutation": {
    "old": "#[inline(always)]\nfn rent_result",
    "new": "\nfn rent_result",
    "hypothesis": "Test normal inlining of the explicit Rent Result argument boundary; it instead leaves an out-of-line helper."
